# Central playground credentials — one local file for every Krokedil plugin.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/krokedil-playground/.env (then `chmod 600` it — the
# copy inherits this committed file's world-readable mode) or merge the
# entries you are missing into your existing file, and fill in what you need;
# leave the rest commented out. Every plugin checkout and worktree reads it — a plugin's
# own gitignored .env overrides it per repo, and ambient env (shell exports,
# CI secrets) wins over everything.
#
# `krokedil-playground credentials` (run in a plugin repo) appends stubs for
# any names that plugin's playground.config.mjs reads but this file lacks.
#
# Sandbox/test credentials only — resolved values land in generated blueprints
# and throwaway playground sites, never use production keys.
#
# Onboarding a plugin? Add its credential names (with a comment saying where
# to obtain them) to this file via PR — see docs/onboarding.md.
#
# Naming: <ABBR>_<OPTION>, where <ABBR> is the plugin's abbreviation
# uppercased — the same identifier behind <ABBR>_LOCAL_DIR and the plugin's
# GitHub secret names. One prefix per plugin, reused as-is: this file is
# shared, so prefixes must not collide, and identical names keep the local
# values and the CI secrets in step. Market suffixes go last (_SE, _EU).
# Abbreviations are assigned in Krokedil's internal CI plugin registry, not in
# this repo; the ones onboarded so far are listed in the README's port
# registry.

# --- krokedil-playground tooling (--tunnel) ---
# Personal authtoken under the Krokedil ngrok pay-as-you-go account
# (dashboard.ngrok.com → Your Authtoken).
# NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=
# One tunnel wp-login password you know, reused across every playground
# (otherwise each --tunnel run prints a random one).
# KROKEDIL_PG_TUNNEL_PASS=

# --- klarna-payments-for-woocommerce ---
# Klarna playground (test) credentials, SE market — obtain from
# portal.playground.klarna.com (Settings → Klarna API credentials / client identifier).
# KP_TEST_MERCHANT_ID_SE=
# KP_TEST_SHARED_SECRET_SE=
# KP_TEST_CLIENT_ID_SE=

# --- qliro-for-woocommerce ---
# Qliro merchant API credentials for the test (sandbox) environment — request
# them from integration@qliro.com, or reuse the pair from the shared Krokedil
# test account. Used when the gateway's "Test mode" is on.
# QLIRO_TEST_API_KEY=
# QLIRO_TEST_API_SECRET=

# --- klarna-checkout-for-woocommerce ---
# Kustom (Klarna) merchant API credentials for the test environment, EU region —
# obtain from the Kustom/Klarna merchant portal (test/playground environment).
# Used when the gateway's "Test mode" is on.
# KCO_TEST_MERCHANT_ID_EU=
# KCO_TEST_SHARED_SECRET_EU=

# --- cargonizer-connect ---
# Logistra Cargonizer sandbox credentials (sandbox.cargonizer.no) — API key
# and sender ID from the Cargonizer sandbox account (Settings → API), profile
# id is the sender profile's id (the plugin requires its external number to
# contain "-W"). Used when the plugin's "Test mode" is on.
# CARGONIZER_TEST_API_KEY=
# CARGONIZER_TEST_SENDER_ID=
# CARGONIZER_TEST_PROFILE_ID=

# --- paytrail-for-woocommerce ---
# Paytrail merchant API credentials — obtain from the Paytrail merchant panel
# (merchant.paytrail.com). Used when the gateway's "Enable test mode" is off;
# with test mode on, the plugin uses Paytrail's built-in public shared test
# credentials instead, so these are only needed for a merchant-specific
# test account.
# PAYTRAIL_TEST_MERCHANT_ID=
# PAYTRAIL_TEST_SECRET_KEY=
